# ── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HTTP_PORT=8080
METRICS_PORT=9090
# Set to false only for local dev without TLS (e.g. running the API with
# `go run` / `make run` behind the plain-http Vite dev proxy). A Secure
# cookie sent over http is silently dropped by the browser, which mints a
# new session on every request. Must stay true (the default) anywhere the
# API is reached over TLS, including staging and production.
COOKIE_SECURE=true

# ── Database (Neon) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL      — direct (non-pooled) endpoint; used by migrations and one-off tools.
# DATABASE_URL_POOLED — PgBouncer (-pooler) endpoint; used by the API.
# Both can be found in the Neon dashboard under "Connection Details".
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>.neon.tech/<dbname>?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL_POOLED=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>-pooler.neon.tech/<dbname>?sslmode=require

# ── Object storage (AWS S3) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev uses the dev stack's buckets (terraform/dev), as staging and
# production use their own: `make dev-deploy`, then copy the S3_* lines
# `make dev-env` prints. Leave the endpoint and keys empty so
# internal/objectstore/s3store authenticates with the AWS credentials below
# (the local IAM user the dev stack grants access to), the way the deployed
# services use their IAM roles.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_BUCKET=dumpster-dev-uploads-<account-id>
S3_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_SECRET_KEY=
S3_USE_PATH_STYLE=false
# Scratch bucket for the hand-off files AWS Batch jobs read and write.
S3_SCRATCH_REGION=us-east-1
S3_SCRATCH_BUCKET=dumpster-dev-scratch-<account-id>
S3_SCRATCH_USE_PATH_STYLE=false

# ── Cloudflare DNS (local-first IaC verification only) ────────────────────────
# Not read by the application itself -- terraform/dns.tf's Cloudflare
# provider picks this up automatically when running `tofu plan`/`apply`
# against terraform/ locally (see CLAUDE.md's IaC verification policy).
# Same variable name as the CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN GitHub Actions secret
# staging.yml passes into CI's own tofu runs.
# Generate one in the Cloudflare dashboard scoped to DNS:Edit on the
# kpednekar.dev zone only -- nothing broader is needed.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=<cloudflare-dns-edit-token>


# ── LLM (AWS Bedrock) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Answers, query routing and canonicalization call Claude through Bedrock,
# authenticated by the AWS credentials below. Set this to the dev stack's
# tagged inference profile (`make dev-env` prints the line) so local usage
# counts as dev spend, not production's. Unset, it falls back to the shared
# us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5 profile.
# Embeddings are generated locally by the inference service (see below), not
# an external API — no embedding-provider key is needed.
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=

# ── Entity extraction (local spaCy + GLiNER) ──────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated, closed-but-broad, domain-agnostic entity type set. Add or
# remove a type here — no code change or migration required.
ENTITY_TYPES=person,organization,location,concept,event,work_of_art,date_time

# ── Inference service ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the consolidated ML inference service: entity extraction, PDF
# region classification, and local embeddings behind one HTTP API. Defaults
# to the docker-compose service name; override for local dev without Docker.
INFERENCE_SERVICE_URL=http://inference:8000

# ── AWS credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From the standard SDK chain. Locally, the keys of an IAM user the dev stack
# grants publish access to (terraform/dev's local_iam_user), also used by
# cmd/reembed's Batch embedding below.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<scoped-batch-user-access-key-id>
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<scoped-batch-user-secret-key>

# ── Batch embedding for cmd/reembed ────────────────────────────────
# Always AWS Batch (internal/llm/awsbatch) — not optional, no HTTP fallback.
# Moved off INFERENCE_SERVICE_URL after measuring Fly's shared-cpu tier
# throttling a 47.5s embedding call into 13-16+ minutes in production; see
# internal/llm/awsbatch's package doc for the full story. Query-time
# embedding (api) is unaffected and still uses INFERENCE_SERVICE_URL above —
# a per-request Batch cold start would be unacceptable for a live search.
# Uses the AWS credentials above, against a CPU-only Fargate compute
# environment.
# EMBED_BATCH_JOB_QUEUE=dumpster-embedding-queue
# EMBED_BATCH_JOB_DEFINITION=dumpster-embedding-jobdef

# Optional — cmd/reembed's Batch polling and presign settings. Default to
# internal/llm/awsbatch's own defaults (5s / 15m) when unset.
# BATCH_POLL_INTERVAL=5s
# BATCH_PRESIGN_TTL=15m

# --- Event-driven pipeline (publishing jobs) ---
# Uploads and retries publish jobs to Step Functions state machines and two
# SQS queues instead of the Postgres jobs table. For local development these
# are the pipeline-only dev stack's (terraform/dev): deploy it with
# `AWS_PROFILE=<your-admin-profile> make dev-deploy`, then paste the lines
# `make dev-env` prints here. The API refuses to start without all five.
#
# Publishing uses the AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY above; the dev
# stack grants that IAM user (terraform/dev's local_iam_user) StartExecution
# on these state machines.
DOCUMENT_INDEXING_STATE_MACHINE_ARN=arn:aws:states:us-east-1:<account-id>:stateMachine:dumpster-dev-document-indexing
ENTITY_EXTRACTION_STATE_MACHINE_ARN=arn:aws:states:us-east-1:<account-id>:stateMachine:dumpster-dev-entity-extraction
REGION_CLASSIFICATION_STATE_MACHINE_ARN=arn:aws:states:us-east-1:<account-id>:stateMachine:dumpster-dev-region-classification
EDGE_EXTRACTION_STATE_MACHINE_ARN=arn:aws:states:us-east-1:<account-id>:stateMachine:dumpster-dev-edge-extraction
CANONICALIZATION_STATE_MACHINE_ARN=arn:aws:states:us-east-1:<account-id>:stateMachine:dumpster-dev-canonicalization
